        <mxCell id="i6__2" value="All 12 direct child instances of m_vlsit_riscv_cluster_core are shown. The top row shows the per-hart AXI route, normal-memory mux and LLC; the middle row shows device egress, maintenance control and LLC service bridge; the bottom row shows PMU, fault record and AXI4-Lite control. Arrows show primary data/control paths and the fault-record CSR path. For legibility, secondary PMU event-source and LLC/L1 fault-source bundles are detailed in HDS Sections 6 and 14 and are not separate arrows here. The route generates four hart slots indexed 0..3; PARA_CPU_NUM activates two or four. Nested CVA6/HPDcache/MESI and internal CCU hierarchy is expanded in Section 14 component diagrams. Signal names and block provenance for shown paths are listed on BLOCK_INFORMATION. Responses return on the same protocol bundle." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;fontSize=18;fontColor=#000000;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1" vlsit_library_sha256="15DFB183E267D2A94F8CAB316E01EB3D2E9D2F9C006DC816790A394F4123506C" vlsit_library_entry="0" vlsit_library_cell="2" vlsit_library_instance="i6">
